title start
kind: module
tags: module
Module page: a piece of code, explained before it is shown
title end

paragraph start
Use a module page to document one piece of code so it can be understood without running it. Say what it is for first, then show it.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Purpose
title end

paragraph start
Say what problem this code solves and what it leaves out. Keep it short. If you cannot state the purpose in a few sentences, the module is doing too much.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Code
title end

paragraph start
The code goes in a code block, with its language written under the start line. Below is a tiny example.
paragraph end

code start
language: racket
(define (greet name)
  (string-append "hello " name))
code end

section end

comment start
a purpose, then the code
comment end

